>> 22 Convert 200 g of sugar and 375°F to cups and Celsius.
[completed 4s run=cmwvpey8j009207p9qjvovh1u] **200 g sugar ≈ 1 cup** — granulated sugar is almost exactly 200 g per cup, so this one converts neatly.

**375°F ≈ 190°C** (190.6°C exactly — for a Portuguese oven, set it to 190°C; if you're baking something delicate like pastéis de nata, 190°C is the standard equivalent).

Useful rule of thumb for sugar by weight: white sugar 200 g/cup, but brown sugar is ~220 g/cup (packed) and icing sugar ~120 g/cup, so always convert by type.
